INT. GRAND HOTEL LOBBY, SNOWED IN - NIGHT

A cavernous lobby of marble and brass. A grand staircase. A dead fireplace. Snow piled against the revolving door. Candles in saucers on every table.

Six people occupy the room. They have not yet spoken to one another.

DETECTIVE RAYMOND OKONKWO-HAYES. 50s. Rumpled. Smokes unlit cigarettes.

LADY EUDORA PEMBERTON-ASANTE. 70s. Pearls. A cane with a silver head.

PROFESSOR ISIDORE KOWALSKI-BRIGHT. 60s. Tweed. Spectacles on a chain.

MISS CALLISTA DEVEREAUX-ADEYEMI. 30s. Evening gown. Scarlet lipstick.

DOCTOR SAMUEL NAKAMURA-OKORO. 40s. Medical bag at his feet.

THE DESK CLERK, ELMER FINNEGAN-LUU. 20s. Terrified.

A scream cuts through the lobby, from upstairs. Everyone freezes. A door slams.

RAYMOND
Nobody move.

EUDORA
I wasn't going to.

RAYMOND
Clerk. Who's on the third floor?

ELMER
Mr. Delacroix, sir. Room 312.

RAYMOND
Key.

Elmer fumbles under the desk. Slides a brass key across the counter. Raymond snatches it and bounds up the stairs. The others stand frozen, until Samuel grabs his bag and follows. Callista watches him go, sets down her glass, and races after, leaving Eudora and Isidore alone with the clerk.

INT. HOTEL - THIRD FLOOR HALLWAY - CONTINUOUS

A long corridor, red carpet. Raymond reaches 312, tries the knob, then shoulder-rams the door. It gives.

INT. HOTEL - ROOM 312 - CONTINUOUS

A man lies face-down on the floor, a candlestick beside him. Samuel kneels and checks his neck.

SAMUEL
Dead.

RAYMOND
How long?

SAMUEL
Minutes.

CALLISTA
(at the door)
Oh, God.

RAYMOND
Miss Devereaux, stay back.

CALLISTA
He was my husband.

Samuel looks up sharply. Raymond turns. In the doorway, behind Callista, the others have gathered: Eudora leaning on her cane, Isidore polishing his spectacles, Elmer trembling.

RAYMOND
Everyone in the room. Nobody leaves.

EUDORA
It was always going to be me or the Professor.

ISIDORE
Lady Pemberton!

EUDORA
Oh, don't be coy, Isidore. We both had reasons.

RAYMOND
What reasons?

EUDORA
He owed us money.

ISIDORE
A great deal of it.

ELMER
(small voice)
He owed me, too.

Raymond looks at each in turn. Samuel rises and wipes his hands. Callista is staring at the floor.

CALLISTA
He owed all of us.

RAYMOND
Then it's a long list.

The lights go out. A candle flame gutters. In the dark, a single gunshot cracks. A woman gasps. Everyone scatters. Raymond throws himself at the doorway, Samuel dives behind the bed, Eudora swings her cane in a wide arc, Isidore ducks under the desk, Elmer bolts for the window, and Callista grabs for the candlestick.

A match flares. Raymond stands over the figure on the floor, the smoking pistol in Eudora's hand.

RAYMOND (CONT'D)
Lady Pemberton. Put it down.

EUDORA
I only shot the lamp, Detective.

She sets the pistol on the dresser and sits on the bed, composed, hands folded.

EUDORA (CONT'D)
I wanted you to see his face when the light came back.

The match gutters out.
